BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: a changed date of a WHOLE-DAY series is written by Google
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:as RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE, with no time in it at all. It has to be matched
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:against the whole-day slot it replaces (a plain date), not turned into a
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:moment first. Read the wrong way it matches nothing, and the calendar shows
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:both the old date and the new one. Three Mondays; the second is moved to the
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:Tuesday, so 19 October must disappear and 20 October take its place.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:allday-override-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261012
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261013
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;COUNT=3
SUMMARY:Whole-day series
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:allday-override-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:Whole-day series (moved to the Tuesday)
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
